        "answer_image": null,
        "explanation": "<p>Uneven drying during air seasoning often leads to <i>warping</i>, where the timber bends or twists due to differential moisture loss. Other defects like <i>checking</i> (surface cracks) or <i>honeycombing</i> (internal cracks) can also occur but are less directly tied to uneven drying.</p>",
